---
import Feature from './Feature.astro';
import Mark from './Mark.astro';
import Shot from './Shot.astro';
---

<section id="features" class="wrap features">
  <Feature
    eyebrow="Memories by band"
    title="Bring your CHIRP file. Every memory lands under its band."
    visualBasis={560}
  >
    Export from CHIRP, import into Leyline, and your memories become named bookmarks with their
    tones, offsets and comments, filed under 2 m, 70 cm and GMRS instead of one long list. Channel
    plans for NOAA weather, GMRS, MURS and marine VHF are built in, so WX3 or GMRS 17 is one click
    with nothing to program.
    <div slot="visual" class="chirp">
      <Shot name="chirp-csv-before" frame="terminal" class="csv" />
      <Shot name="sidebar-chirp-import" class="after" />
    </div>
  </Feature>

  <Feature eyebrow="Tone discovery" title="Hear a repeater, learn its tone." flip visualBasis={480}>
    On an NFM channel Leyline listens under the voice for a CTCSS tone or a DCS code and shows it
    beside the bookmark’s tone, the way your radio’s menu would: PL 127.3, or DCS 023 in octal. Add
    it to the bookmark, then program your handheld.
    <div slot="visual" class="pair">
      <Shot name="inspector-tone" />
      <Shot name="inspector-dcs" />
    </div>
  </Feature>

  <Feature eyebrow="Scanning" title="Sweep a band and see what’s on it." stacked>
    A scan lists each carrier with its frequency, width, signal-to-noise and how often it was seen,
    so a single burst reads differently from a repeater that is always up. It reports what it
    measured and doesn’t guess the mode. In the app, Scan band lists the hits under the band and
    marks them on the band rail. If someone is already listening on the radio, it says so instead of
    taking over.
    <div slot="visual" class="stack">
      <Shot name="scan-2m" frame="terminal" />
      <Shot name="scan-app" />
    </div>
  </Feature>

  <Feature eyebrow="Auto-recording" title="Every over, its own clip." flip visualBasis={560}>
    With the squelch as the gate, Leyline records only while someone is on the air, and keeps half a
    second before each transmission so no clip starts mid-word. Leave a net running and come back to
    a list of transmissions instead of an hour of hiss.
    <Shot slot="visual" name="library-net" />
  </Feature>

  <Feature eyebrow="Decoding" title="APRS, weather alerts and AIS, decoded." stacked>
    Decoders share the radio with you when their channel is in range, or run on a second radio.
    Follow APRS stations as they beacon, see vessels on AIS, and set a watch that sends a macOS
    notification when a SAME alert names your county. Alerts can also go to a webhook or a shell
    command.
    <div slot="visual" class="stack">
      <div class="notif mac">
        <span class="notif-icon">
          <Mark size={20} />
        </span>
        <div class="notif-body">
          <div class="notif-top">
            <span class="notif-title">Severe Thunderstorm Warning</span>
            <span class="when">now</span>
          </div>
          <span class="where">Fairfax County, VA, until 21:45</span>
          <span class="src">SAME on NOAA WX2 · 162.400 MHz</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <Shot name="aprs-track" frame="terminal" />
      <Shot name="ais-track" frame="terminal" />
    </div>
  </Feature>
</section>

<style>
  .features {
    padding-top: 140px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 120px;
  }

  .mac {
    font-family: var(--font-mac);
  }

  .stack {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 1000px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 14px;
  }

  /* The CHIRP export, then the sidebar it became, overlapping it. */
  .chirp {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .chirp :global(.csv) {
    width: 90%;
  }

  .chirp :global(.after) {
    width: 72%;
    margin: -96px 0 0 auto;
    box-shadow: 0 30px 60px -20px rgb(0 0 0 / 90%);
  }

  .pair {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 14px;
  }

  /* Decoding */
  .notif {
    align-self: flex-end;
    width: min(100%, 370px);
    display: flex;
    gap: 12px;
    padding: 14px;
    border-radius: 16px;
    background: rgb(40 44 48 / 92%);
    border: 1px solid #33393d;
    box-shadow: 0 24px 50px -20px rgb(0 0 0 / 90%);
  }

  .notif-icon {
    width: 36px;
    height: 36px;
    flex: none;
    border-radius: 9px;
    background: var(--bg);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .notif-body {
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2px;
    font-size: 13px;
  }

  .notif-top {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .notif-title {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text-bright);
  }

  .when {
    font-size: 11.5px;
    color: var(--muted-2);
  }

  .where {
    color: #d5d8da;
  }

  .src {
    color: var(--muted-2);
    font-size: 12px;
  }
</style>
